.TH "observe_init" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

void observe_init(int fd, int level);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initializes the per\-session observability subsystem.
Sets the file descriptor used for sending observe events to the client,
resets the event sequence counter to zero, and clears all internal state
(timing, hook registration).
.PP
If \f[B]level\f[R] is greater than 0, \f[CR]observe_init()\f[R] calls
\f[CR]observe_set_level()\f[R] to register the appropriate command hooks
immediately.
.PP
This function is called after authentication completes in the v2 session
handler (\f[CR]json_session_handle()\f[R]).
Because bash\-server uses a fork\-per\-session model, the module\-level
globals (\f[CR]observe_fd\f[R], \f[CR]observe_level\f[R],
\f[CR]event_seq\f[R], etc.)
are safely per\-process.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]fd\f[R] \(em File descriptor for writing observe frames to the
client.
Must be a valid writable fd (typically the session\(cqs write fd).
Passed directly to \f[CR]json_frame_write_fmt()\f[R] when emitting
events.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]level\f[R] \(em Desired observability level.
Valid values:
.RS 2
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]0\f[R] (\f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_OFF\f[R]): No event hooks;
output\-only mode.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]1\f[R] (\f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_COMMAND\f[R]): Pre/post command events
with command string, cwd, line number, subshell/async flags, exit
status, signal number, and duration.
.PP
Values above \f[CR]OBSERVE_LEVEL_MAX\f[R] are clamped by
\f[CR]observe_set_level()\f[R].
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
None.
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]observe_cleanup\f[R](3), \f[CR]observe_set_level\f[R](3),
\f[CR]json_frame_write_fmt\f[R](3), \f[CR]json_session_handle\f[R](3)
.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The observe fd is \f[B]not\f[R] closed by \f[CR]observe_cleanup()\f[R].
The caller (session handler) owns the fd lifetime.
.IP \(bu 2
Event sequence numbers (\f[CR]event_seq\f[R]) start at 0 for each
session and increment monotonically across all event types.
.IP \(bu 2
Calling \f[CR]observe_init()\f[R] a second time within the same process
resets all state, including unregistering any previously registered
hooks (implicitly, by resetting \f[CR]hooks_registered\f[R] to 0 before
\f[CR]observe_set_level()\f[R] re\-registers them).
